# ============================================================
#  Incidents and money sinks (design §8.2).
#  A) forced sinks: setbacks that cost crowns or health, always
#     with a way to soften them. Gated on gold so they drain
#     savings rather than break poor players.
#  B) voluntary sinks: patronage and donations for the well-off.
#  C) year three: a term of Thornwick exchange students.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- A) Forced sinks ----------------

@event inc_fever_bill
time: morning
title: A Fever and a Bill
class: incident
tone: tense
when: turn >= 3 and gold >= 30 and seen(inc_fever_bill) < 2 and since(inc_fever_bill) >= 12
weight: 6
repeat: 2
art: potion
tags: life money
scene: A pale student in an infirmary bed, a stern nurse holding out a small blue bottle and a folded bill.
text: You wake in the infirmary with a fever that makes the ceiling breathe. Sister Amaranth holds up a small blue bottle. "This clears it by morning. It is also not free," she says. "Or you can sweat it out, like your ancestors."
> left: Buy the tonic
  gold -large
  health -small
  say: {~It tastes of tin and regret.|It tastes like a pond that has given up.} By morning the ceiling is a ceiling again, and your purse is noticeably lighter.
> right: Sweat it out
  health -medium
  study -small
  say: Three days of damp sheets and strange dreams about stairs. You miss a week of notes, and come back feeling like a wrung-out dishcloth.

@event inc_broken_wand
title: Snapped on the Stairs
class: incident
tone: tense
when: turn >= 3 and gold >= 30 and seen(inc_broken_wand) == 0
weight: 6
repeat: 1
art: wand
tags: magic money
scene: A student kneeling on a stone staircase, holding the two halves of a wand that still fizzes faintly at the break.
text: The moving stairs shift without warning. You catch yourself; your wand doesn't. It lies in two pieces on the landing, still fizzing at the break like a sulking firework.
> left: Have it properly rebound
  gold -large
  say: The repairer in the village tuts, splints it with silver wire and charges you for every tut. It works better than before, which is somehow worse.
> right: Bind it with string and hope
  challenge spell apprentice wild:
    win:
      mood -tiny
      say: It holds. It spits a little when you cast, like a cat that forgives you but wants it noted.
    lose:
      health -small
      study -small
      say: It holds for three days, then sneezes a spell backwards. Your eyebrows grow back within the week; your marks take longer.

@event inc_library_fine
title: The Overdue Notice
class: incident
tone: light
when: turn >= 3 and gold >= 30 and seen(inc_library_fine) < 2 and since(inc_library_fine) >= 12
weight: 6
repeat: 2
art: paper
tags: study money
scene: A prefect in a red sash holding out a long paper notice, a book with teeth marks on the desk between them.
text: A prefect in a red sash slides a notice across your desk. The library book you borrowed has come back late, damp and, somehow, with teeth marks. "Damages," she says. "Or you can argue. People do. It never goes well."
> left: Pay the fine
  gold -medium
  mood -tiny
  say: She stamps your receipt with great satisfaction. The book is reshelved in a cage, which feels like the right outcome for everyone.
> right: Argue that the book bit first
  challenge negotiate apprentice+ unlikely:
    win:
      mood +tiny
      say: You produce the bite on your thumb as evidence. The prefect inspects it, then the book, and waives the fine. "Fair," she says. "It has a history."
    lose:
      gold -large
      study -tiny
      say: The prefect writes down every word you say, then doubles the fine for "contempt of librarian". You pay it, and lose an evening's revision to the demerit hearing besides.

@event inc_letter_home
title: Bad Weather at Home
class: incident
tone: grim
when: turn >= 3 and gold >= 30 and seen(inc_letter_home) == 0
weight: 6
repeat: 1
art: letter
tags: home money
scene: A student at a window reading a rain-spotted letter, a small pile of coins on the sill beside them.
text: A letter from home, written in a hurry. A storm took half the roof, and the repairs will cost more than anyone has. Nobody asks you for anything. That's how you know it's bad.
> left: Send crowns home
  gold -large
  alignment +small
  mood -small
  say: You send everything you can spare and a little you can't. The reply comes a month later: a drawing of a roof, finished, and a pressed flower.
> right: Write back with love, not money
  mood -medium
  say: You write four pages and keep your purse. The reply is kind. It doesn't mention the roof. That night you lie awake and listen to the rain.

@event inc_stolen_purse
title: Market Day Fingers
class: incident
tone: tense
when: turn >= 3 and gold >= 30 and seen(inc_stolen_purse) < 2 and since(inc_stolen_purse) >= 12
weight: 6
repeat: 2
art: pouch
tags: money danger
scene: A crowded village square on market day, a figure in a grey hood slipping away between the stalls with a small purse.
text: Somewhere between the cheese stall and the man selling enchanted socks, your purse stops being yours. You catch a grey hood slipping between the stalls, already three stalls ahead.
> left: Run after the hood
  challenge feat apprentice+:
    win:
      gold -tiny
      health -tiny
      say: You corner the thief behind the bakery. The purse comes back a little lighter; they'd already spent some on a bun. You let them keep the bun.
    lose:
      gold -large
      health -small
      mood -small
      say: You trip over a goose, then a second goose. When you get up, the hood is gone, and so are your crowns.
> right: Let it go
  gold -large
  mood -small
  say: You tell yourself it's only money. You tell yourself that all the way back up the hill, and it never quite takes.

@event inc_hiccuping_robe
time: morning
title: The Robe That Hiccups
class: incident
tone: light
when: turn >= 3 and gold >= 20 and seen(inc_hiccuping_robe) == 0
weight: 6
repeat: 1
art: cauldron
tags: magic money
scene: A student in potion-stained robes jolting mid-step as their robe gives a visible hiccup, classmates hiding smiles.
text: A cauldron two benches down boils over, and a whole batch of Draught of Unending Hiccups soaks your best robe. The stain fades by supper. The hiccups don't. Every few minutes, the robe jumps.
> left: Buy a new robe
  gold -medium
  mood -tiny
  say: The tailor in the village fits you in an afternoon and charges you for a week. The old robe now hiccups quietly in the bottom of your trunk.
> right: Wear it with dignity
  renown -small
  mood -small
  say: {~It hiccups through a lecture on silence.|It hiccups through the headmistress's announcements.} Someone starts a tally on the common-room wall. You are briefly famous for the wrong reasons.

# ---------------- B) Voluntary sinks: patronage ----------------

@event patron_tournament_purse
title: A Patron's Purse
class: routine
tone: light
when: (month == 7 or month == 8) and gold >= 80
weight: 10
repeat: 12
art: trophy
tags: festival money
scene: A festival committee table on a lawn, a thin purse on a velvet cushion and a list of patrons with plenty of space left.
text: The Spring Tournament committee has a velvet cushion, a very thin prize purse and a list of patrons with a lot of room left on it. Patrons are read out before the first bout, in a loud voice, to the whole academy.
> left: Fund the champion's purse
  gold -large
  renown +medium
  say: {~Your name is read out first, and mispronounced only slightly.|Your name rings across the lawn before the first bout. Two first-years bow to you, unsure why.} The champion thanks you from the podium.
> right: Cheer from the stands instead
  mood +tiny
  say: Other names are read out, among them a professor's cat and "a well-wisher". You cheer for all of them, and loudest for the champion.

@event patron_ledger_print
title: Paper for the Press
class: routine
tone: light
when: turn >= 6 and gold >= 80
weight: 6
repeat: 12
art: paper
tags: social money
scene: A cramped office under a staircase, a groaning printing press, and a young editor holding out an empty paper tray.
text: Nessa Quill corners you by the library stairs, holding an empty paper tray like evidence. "Special edition. Biggest story of the term. No paper. You," she says, pointing, "look solvent. Patrons get their name on the masthead."
> left: Pay for the whole print run
  gold -large
  rel nessa +medium
  renown +medium
  say: "Headline: generous student saves free press," Nessa says, already writing it. The masthead lists you in tiny capitals, which she says is the most honour anyone gets.
> right: Help her fold the edition instead
  rel nessa +small
  health -tiny
  say: You'd rather give her your time than your crowns. Nessa scrounges paper from the Ledger's scrap bin, and you fold until midnight, fingers grey with ink. Nessa credits you on the back page as "the folding department".

# ---------------- B) Voluntary sinks: donations ----------------

@event donate_greenhouse_glass
time: morning
title: The Broken Panes
class: routine
tone: warm
when: turn >= 3 and gold >= 80 and not discovered(greenhouses)
weight: 8
repeat: 3
art: leaf
tags: nature money
scene: A collection tin on a garden gate, broken glass glittering in the grass behind it and steam escaping from a damaged greenhouse.
text: Last night's hail went through the greenhouse glass like a hammer through toffee. A collection tin hangs on the gate with a hand-lettered sign: every pane paid for keeps the mandrakes from catching cold.
> left: Pay for a whole pane
  gold -large
  mood +small
  discover greenhouses
  say: A gardener with mud to the elbows insists on showing you your pane. Inside it is warm, green and loud with opinions. You are welcome, she says, any morning.
> right: Walk on
  mood -tiny
  say: You walk past the tin. Behind the gate, something small and leafy sneezes. You feel, obscurely, that you've been judged.

@event donate_duel_floor
title: The Scorched Floor
class: routine
tone: light
when: turn >= 3 and gold >= 80 and not discovered(duel_hall)
weight: 8
repeat: 3
art: sword
tags: club money
scene: A sweaty duellist with a collection box at the foot of a stair, scorched floorboards stacked behind them.
text: A duellist with a bandaged hand rattles a box at the foot of the east stair. "The hall floor," he says. "Someone set it on fire again. Every board you buy, we carve your initials on the underside. Honour, and splinters."
> left: Buy a row of floorboards
  gold -large
  renown +small
  discover duel_hall
  say: He drags you upstairs to see. The hall smells of smoke and wax, and the practice dummies glare at you. Your initials go on the underside of the board by the door.
> right: Wish him luck with the bandage
  mood -tiny
  say: He thanks you with exaggerated courtesy and goes back to rattling. Somewhere above, steel rings on steel, and nobody invites you up.

# ---------------- C) Year three: the Thornwick exchange ----------------

@event xchg_arrival
title: Guests in Green
class: routine
tone: light
when: year == 3 and month <= 2 and seen(xchg_arrival) == 0
weight: 12
art: mask
tags: social rival
scene: Four students in green Thornwick robes standing in a grand entrance hall, the portraits on the walls all turned to stare at them.
text: Four students in Thornwick green arrive for a term, with trunks and very polite smiles. Within an hour every portrait in the entrance hall is winking at the wrong people. A prefect looks around for someone, anyone, to show them the castle.
> left: Offer to show them round
  challenge appeal apprentice+:
    win:
      renown +small
      charm +small
      say: You give the full tour, moving stairs included. By the end the boy with the sketchbook admits Lumenhold's towers are "not as crooked as reported".
    lose:
      mood -small
      renown -tiny
      say: Halfway round, they convince you a wall is a door. It isn't. They are very sorry, and laughing too hard to say so.
> right: Watch them from a distance
  guile +small
  say: You watch them all week. They watch back. You learn that the quiet one counts doorways, and that they know you're watching.

@event xchg_ink_cuffs
title: The Ink-Stained Cuffs
class: routine
tone: tense
when: year == 3 and month <= 4 and seen(xchg_arrival) > 0 and seen(xchg_farewell) == 0
weight: 12
art: book
tags: study rival
scene: A library at dusk, a student in green robes with ink-stained cuffs copying from a book chained to a desk.
text: Late in the library, you find the Thornwick girl with the ink-stained cuffs copying from a chained book she shouldn't have reached. She sees you see her. "It's only history," she says. "Unless you want it to be a scandal."
> left: Report her to the librarian
  renown +small
  mood -small
  say: The librarian thanks you, coldly. The Thornwick girl is confined to the guest wing for a week. She nods to you at dinner afterwards, as if you had both played well.
> right: Keep quiet, for a favour
  alignment -tiny
  guile +small
  say: She tears out the page she copied and hands you the other half of her notes instead. "We're even," she says. You're fairly sure you aren't.

@event xchg_farewell
title: A Thornwick Farewell
class: milestone
tone: warm
when: year == 3 and month <= 4 and seen(xchg_arrival) > 0 and since(xchg_arrival) >= 2 and seen(xchg_farewell) == 0
weight: 12
art: group
tags: social rival
scene: Students in green and blue robes on a jetty at dawn, a barge waiting, one of them holding out a striped scarf.
text: The Thornwick students leave on today's barge. The boy with the sketchbook finds you on the jetty and holds out his scarf. "It's a custom," he says. "Probably. I've just decided." Behind him his friends pretend not to listen.
> left: Swap scarves
  mood +medium
  renown -tiny
  say: You trade scarves on the jetty. Someone from your own house mutters "traitor" at breakfast. You wear it anyway, and get a letter from across the hills by the end of the month.
> right: Challenge him to one last duel
  challenge combat adept- wild:
    win:
      renown +medium
      say: You win, narrowly, on the wet boards. He laughs, bows, and sketches you mid-spell on the barge as it pulls away. The sketch arrives by post, flattering.
    lose:
      health -small
      mood +small
      say: He wins with an illusion of a second you. You both end up in the lake. It is, somehow, the best goodbye you've had.
